PREAMBLE

The SWORD Restricted Source Licence ("SRSL") is a source-available software licence intended to encourage independent research, education, experimentation and non-commercial development while preserving the copyright holder's exclusive control over commercial exploitation.

The Software is provided freely for eligible non-commercial purposes. Commercial exploitation is not authorised by this Licence and requires a separate written agreement with the Licensor.

The Licensor may offer commercial licensing under substantial financial and source-disclosure obligations or negotiate alternative arrangements at its sole discretion.

This Licence is not an open-source licence as defined by the Open Source Initiative.

1. DEFINITIONS

1.1 "Software" means the source code, object code, documentation, associated files and modifications expressly distributed under SRSL-1.0.

1.2 "Licensor" means the copyright holder or other person legally authorised to grant rights in the Software.

1.3 "Licensee" means any individual or legal entity exercising rights granted by this Licence.

1.4 "Non-Commercial Use" means use primarily for personal, educational, academic, experimental, charitable or independent research purposes, without direct or indirect commercial exploitation of the Software.

Incidental personal benefits, including learning, skill development, portfolio development and improved employment prospects, do not alone constitute Commercial Exploitation.

1.5 "Commercial Exploitation" means use of the Software substantially connected with obtaining revenue, fees, commercial advantage, business cost savings or other measurable economic benefit for a commercial enterprise.

This includes, without limitation:
- Incorporation into commercial products or services.
- Provision of paid analysis, consultancy or processing services using the Software.
- Commercial hosting or software-as-a-service deployments.
- Internal business deployment for operational or economic advantage.
- Incorporation into proprietary software distributed commercially.
- Commercial redistribution, sublicensing or sale.
- Commercial research or development intended to produce commercially exploitable products or services.

The mere status of an organisation as a commercial entity does not automatically establish Commercial Exploitation; the actual purpose and circumstances of use shall determine classification.

1.6 "Modification" means any adaptation, alteration, extension or derivative work of the Software to the extent recognised by applicable copyright law.

1.7 "Commercial Agreement" means a separate written agreement, executed by the Licensor and the relevant commercial licensee, expressly granting specified commercial rights.

1.8 "Covered Product" means the product, service, application or system expressly identified in a Commercial Agreement as incorporating or exploiting the Software.

2. GRANT OF NON-COMMERCIAL RIGHTS

Subject to compliance with this Licence, the Licensor grants the Licensee a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free, non-transferable licence to:

a. Download and reproduce the Software.
b. Inspect, study and analyse its source code.
c. Compile and execute the Software.
d. Modify, extend and adapt the Software.
e. Use the Software in personal laboratories, home computing environments and independent non-commercial projects.
f. Use the Software for eligible educational and academic activities.
g. Redistribute original or modified copies for Non-Commercial Use, provided all applicable copyright notices, licence terms and attribution requirements remain intact.

No registration, payment or prior approval is required for activities expressly permitted by this section.

This grant is limited to Non-Commercial Use and remains subject to the restrictions below.

3. RESTRICTIONS ON COMMERCIAL EXPLOITATION

No permission for Commercial Exploitation is granted under SRSL-1.0.

A Licensee must obtain a separate Commercial Agreement before commencing Commercial Exploitation of the Software.

Without such an agreement, the Licensee must not:

a. Incorporate the Software into commercial products or services.
b. Deploy the Software for material commercial advantage.
c. Sell, rent, license or commercially redistribute the Software or covered derivative works.
d. Offer paid access to functionality substantially provided by the Software.
e. Use the Software as part of commercial analysis, processing or research services.
f. Grant commercial sublicences to third parties.
g. Represent possession of the source code as authorisation for commercial exploitation.

Commercial use without appropriate authorisation may constitute copyright infringement or another actionable violation, subject to applicable law.

Nothing in this section prohibits activities permitted by mandatory statutory provisions that cannot lawfully be excluded.

4. COMMERCIAL LICENSING

4.1 No Automatic Commercial Licence

Commercial rights are granted only through a separately executed Commercial Agreement.

Publication of standard commercial terms does not itself grant commercial rights, establish a contractual relationship or create an automatic obligation to pay royalties.

4.2 Standard Commercial Licensing Proposal

Unless otherwise negotiated, the Licensor's standard opening proposal for commercial licensing comprises:

A. Profit Participation

Payment to the Licensor of fifty percent (50%) of Defined Attributable Net Profits arising from the authorised commercial exploitation of the Software.

Defined Attributable Net Profits shall be calculated using the accounting methodology expressly agreed in the Commercial Agreement.

The agreement shall specify:
- Revenue attributable to the Covered Product.
- Permitted direct costs and deductions.
- Treatment of related-party transactions.
- Accounting periods and reporting obligations.
- Treatment of losses and adjustments.
- Procedures for resolving accounting disputes.

Where commercial benefit cannot reasonably be measured through product profits, the Licensor may propose an alternative fee or royalty structure.

B. Complete Covered-Product Source Disclosure

The commercial licensee shall provide the Licensor with complete, corresponding source code for the Covered Product, to the extent specified in the Commercial Agreement.

This may include:
- Modifications to the Software.
- Proprietary components incorporated into the Covered Product.
- Integration and interface code.
- Build scripts and configuration required to reproduce the licensed functionality.
- Other source material expressly identified in the agreement.

Disclosure obligations shall respect third-party intellectual-property rights and applicable law.

Disclosure does not automatically transfer copyright or grant redistribution rights to the Licensor.

C. Financial Transparency

The commercial licensee shall maintain accurate records sufficient to calculate and verify royalties.

The Commercial Agreement may require periodic financial statements and reasonable independent audits, subject to appropriate confidentiality and data-protection safeguards.

D. Commercial Restrictions

Unless expressly authorised in writing, commercial licences shall not permit sublicensing, assignment, transfer or expansion beyond the agreed products, services, territories or activities.

4.3 Additional Negotiated Conditions

The Licensor may request additional contractual obligations, including broader source-code disclosure, enhanced auditing, minimum payments or other commercially negotiated conditions.

Such obligations apply only where expressly agreed in a valid Commercial Agreement.

4.4 Alternative Commercial Terms

The Licensor may negotiate alternative commercial arrangements, including:
- Fixed licence fees.
- Reduced or increased royalties.
- Subscription or annual licensing.
- Per-product or per-deployment fees.
- Limited-purpose commercial permissions.
- Alternative source-disclosure arrangements.
- Custom enterprise licensing.

The Licensor is under no obligation to offer, approve or negotiate a Commercial Agreement.

5. MODIFICATIONS AND REDISTRIBUTION

Licensees may create and use Modifications for Non-Commercial Use.

Redistribution of the Software or Modifications under this Licence is permitted only where:

a. The redistribution is non-commercial.
b. A copy of SRSL-1.0 accompanies the redistributed material.
c. Existing copyright and attribution notices are preserved.
d. Material modifications are identified as such.
e. Recipients are informed that Commercial Exploitation requires separate authorisation.
f. The redistributor has sufficient rights to distribute any third-party material included.

No Licensee may represent a modified version as an official SWORD release without authorisation.

Nothing in this section requires a Licensee to publish private non-commercial modifications.

