To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, the Software is provided "AS IS" and "AS AVAILABLE", without warranties of merchantability, satisfactory quality, fitness for a particular purpose, non-infringement or uninterrupted operation.

The Licensee assumes responsibility for determining the Software's suitability for its intended use.

Nothing in this Licence excludes warranties or statutory protections that cannot lawfully be excluded.

10. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY

To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, the Licensor shall not be liable for indirect, incidental, consequential or special losses arising from the use or inability to use the Software, including loss of profits, data or business opportunity.

Nothing in this Licence excludes or limits liability for fraud, fraudulent misrepresentation, death or personal injury caused by negligence, or any other liability that cannot lawfully be excluded or limited.

11. STATUTORY RIGHTS

Nothing in this Licence is intended to exclude, restrict or override rights that cannot lawfully be excluded under applicable legislation.

This includes relevant mandatory provisions of the Copyright, Designs and Patents Act 1988, applicable consumer-protection legislation and other mandatory legal rights.

Where a provision conflicts with mandatory law, that provision shall apply only to the maximum extent lawfully permitted.

12. SEVERABILITY

If any provision of this Licence is determined to be unlawful, invalid or unenforceable, the remaining provisions shall continue in effect to the extent legally permissible.

No invalid provision shall be interpreted as granting commercial rights that are otherwise expressly withheld.

13. GOVERNING LAW AND JURISDICTION

This Licence shall be governed by the laws of England and Wales, subject to applicable mandatory legal protections and conflict-of-laws rules.

Subject to any mandatory jurisdictional requirements, disputes arising from this Licence shall be submitted to the courts of England and Wales.

Separate Commercial Agreements may establish their own governing law and dispute-resolution arrangements.

